  "id": "stimulusresponse-compatibility",
  "term": "stimulus–response compatibility",
  "definition": "Stimulus–response compatibility is an effect in which what a person observes automatically affects how they carry out a motor response. In this context, seeing an action can directly influence the performance of one’s own action.",
